WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.186 --> 00:00:02.769
(bright music)

00:00:04.814 --> 00:00:08.731
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.610
- [Narrator] The Zapotecs are the main

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.300
indigenous group living in Oaxaca, Mexico.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.230
Once a thriving civilization
of the pre-Colonial era,

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:41.430
they still keep their
traditions very much alive.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.170
Introducing Zapotecan Abigail Mendoza,

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.323
one of Mexico's most respectable chefs.

00:00:47.471 --> 00:00:51.388
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.380
Cooking since the age of 5, she has become

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.600
world famous for keeping the ancestral

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.503
and traditional Zapotecan
ways of cooking alive.

00:01:09.884 --> 00:01:13.801
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.200
With these tools, Abigail is making dishes

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.580
like the seguesa, a pre-Hispanic mole,

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.323
which has a corn-based
sauce, chilies and turkey.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.950
She also cooks chilies directly on coal,

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.000
stuffed with squash blossom seeds,

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.830
and topped with a melted Oaxacan cheese.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:56.860
And these are all foods

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.843
that were eaten thousands of years ago.

00:02:02.662 --> 00:02:06.662
(speaking in foreign language)

